Q: Using jq, how can I limit values based on a key A: <p>Using <code>from_entries</code>, this worked for me:</p>
<pre><code>$ jq '.employees[] | {number: .number, tags: .tags | from_entries} | select(.tags.management==&quot;no&quot;) | {number: .number, name: .tags.name, login: .tags.login}' input
</code></pre>
<p>... and the output is:</p>
<pre class="lang-json prettyprint-override"><code>{
  &quot;number&quot;: &quot;102&quot;,
  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;jane blogs&quot;,
  &quot;login&quot;: &quot;jane&quot;
}
{
  &quot;number&quot;: &quot;103&quot;,
  &quot;name&quot;: &quot;john doe&quot;,
  &quot;login&quot;: &quot;john&quot;
}
</code></pre>
<p>There may be a better way to achieve what I wanted, so I'll leave the question open for a while if someone wants to offer a better solution.</p>

Q: Using &quot;this-&gt;member_variable&quot; as template function parameter A: <p>If you create a member function with the same name you can pass <code>this</code> as the last argument without updating the call site:</p>
<pre><code>void LOG(Ts&amp;&amp;... ts) {
    ::LOG(tag{}, std::forward&lt;Ts&gt;(ts)..., this);
}
</code></pre>
<p><code>tag</code> is to let <code>LOG</code> know that it has to treat its last element special. Then you can get the last element and use it:</p>
<pre><code>struct tag {};

template&lt;class... Ts&gt;
struct LOG {
    LOG(const char* str, Ts&amp;&amp;... ts):
      LOG(tag{}, str, std::forward&lt;Ts&gt;(ts)..., nullptr) {}

    LOG(tag, const char* str, Ts&amp;&amp;... ts) {
        auto* parent = ts...[sizeof...(ts) - 1];
        if (parent) std::cout &lt;&lt; parent-&gt;m_member;
    }
};
</code></pre>
<p><a href="https://godbolt.org/z/WKoxr5vrv" rel="nofollow noreferrer">Full code:</a></p>
<pre><code>struct tag {};

template&lt;class... Ts&gt;
struct LOG {
    LOG(const char* str, Ts&amp;&amp;... ts):
      LOG(tag{}, str, std::forward&lt;Ts&gt;(ts)..., nullptr) {}

    LOG(tag, const char* str, Ts&amp;&amp;... ts) {
        auto* parent = ts...[sizeof...(ts) - 1];
        if (parent) std::cout &lt;&lt; parent-&gt;m_member;
    }
};

struct A {
    int m_member = 5;
    template&lt;class... Ts&gt;
    void LOG(Ts&amp;&amp;... ts) {
        ::LOG(tag{}, std::forward&lt;Ts&gt;(ts)..., this);
    }
    void foo() {
        LOG(&quot;hello&quot;, 73);
    }
};
</code></pre>
